  "text": "Recipe: Oats Wheat Puttu\nCreator: Saritha Valiyaparambil\nCategory: Puttu\nIngredients: oats flour, whole wheat flour, water, salt, shredded coconut, shredded carrot, shredded beetroot\nCooking methods: mix, steam\nInstructions: Add oat flour and wheat flour with salt & water solution, as needed. Mix well.\nIn a Puttu Maker (a cylindrical steamer), make alternate layers of shredded coconut [or carrot or beetroot] and flour. First, put coconut [or carrot or beetroot], followed by flour and so on.\nSteam until cooked well — approx. 5 to 7 minutes (depends on the quantity of flour).\nNotes: Puttu Maker is a cylindrical steamer. Cooking time approx. 5 to 7 minutes (depends on the quantity of flour).",
